  "body": "Reported by a user in chat on 2026-11-07; filed by an agent.\n\nOpening a user-supplied `.camproj` project pins one CPU core at 100% in the windowed UI. The local file has one 2D Adaptive operation with 2,106 cached moves and 798 warnings, a 2,088-facet model, and one box stock. `camcraft-cli process` completes in under a second, so the expensive path appears to be the windowed shell rather than project parsing or headless generation.\n\nThe shell currently uses `ControlFlow::Poll` and unconditionally requests a redraw in `about_to_wait`. The frame also rebuilds scene data and browser state. Diagnose which frame phase is responsible with its `gpu: slow frame` log, then make idle display responsive without spinning a core. A regression should cover the scheduling or derived-data behavior that caused the report.\n\nThe reporter's project file is local and should not be uploaded without their permission.\n",
